  "evidence": "TEXT_G: NHS Protection Act and compensation for the contaminated blood scandal; end austerity, uprate benefits, protect the pension triple lock and restore Pension Credit; veterans’ housing and benefits and use of vacant MoD homes for homeless veterans; maintain cross‑border security cooperation and retain bases/regiments; crack down on tax avoidance/evasion and reform Companies House; protect the Human Rights Act/ECHR and extend voting to 16–17‑year‑olds; climate targets to net zero by 2045 with green incentives but oppose fracking/new nuclear. TEXT_C: Universal Basic Income and £12 Living Wage (including for ages 16–21), rent controls, free home social care, NHS +£6bn, end no‑fault evictions, write off recent student debt; legalise cannabis, pardons for minor possession/supply, safe consumption rooms, shift to restorative justice; cancel Trident replacement and end arms export promotion; proportional representation, citizens’ assemblies, elected second chamber, a People’s Constitution; rising Carbon Tax, bans on single‑use plastics, near‑100% recycling, end new runways, end ICE car sales by 2030; Consolidated Income Tax on wealth like work, higher Corporation Tax, and a Land Value Tax.",
  "reasoning": "Both texts strongly invoke Care and Equality, but TEXT_G also foregrounds Loyalty and Authority in ways closer to the electorate’s mid‑level weighting (veterans’ support, retaining bases/regiments, and maintaining security tools) while keeping institutional reforms more moderate. TEXT_C places heavier emphasis on Sanctity/Purity and sweeping egalitarian and institutional changes (UBI, broad green bans, drug legalisation, Trident cancellation), which misalign with the electorate’s moderate Authority and Loyalty priorities and low Sanctity weight.",
